# 000 — Core Invariants & Strict Quality Constraints

## 1. Zero Placeholders & Truncated Code
- NEVER emit code containing `// TODO`, `/* rest of code */`, `// ...`, or partial diff snippets.
- Every generated file, function, and test must be complete, functional, and compilable immediately.

## 2. Strict Type Safety & No Bypasses
- NEVER use `any`, `@ts-ignore`, `@ts-nocheck`, or blind type assertions (`as unknown as T`).
- Always validate external inputs using deterministic runtime parsers (Zod, Valibot, Pydantic, etc.).

## 3. Strict Query Bounding
- NEVER execute unbounded database queries (`SELECT *` without `.limit()`).
- All collection scans, search queries, and table reads must define explicit pagination limits (default $\le 50$) and indexed sort orders.
